abstract: >-
  This work characterizes how corpus composition and retrieval architecture
  jointly affect RAG security. We find that technical corpora are 13-62×
  harder to defend than general knowledge bases, and that simple hybrid
  BM25+vector retrieval neutralizes gradient-optimized attacks. Key findings
  include 38% co-retrieval success on pure vector retrieval (n=50), 0%
  success with hybrid retrieval (α≤0.5), 60% end-to-end LLM attack success
  with 80% safety bypass rate, and validation of corpus-dependency through
  production RAG case study (156,777 documents).
